<title>ISRAEL: ISRAEL GRAIN, MEAL, SOY ARRIVALS DETAILED.</title>
<headline>ISRAEL GRAIN, MEAL, SOY ARRIVALS DETAILED.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Sormovsky 10     unloading   barley	    2,745     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobalt 238    arrived     barley	    2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Volgodon 5035    arrived     rapeseed	  3,600     Europe</p>
<p>Aston Prelude    arrived     wheat	     3,310     Europe</p>
<p>Iyoanis P	  arrived     corn	     16,326     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     14,476</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  31,335</p>
<p>Malanga	    12/8	  rapeseed meal   3,000     n/a</p>
<p>Sormovsky 3066   14/8	  wheat	     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Flag Mersindi    14/8	  soya meal	 7,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn		8,766</p>
<p>				     barley	    3,091</p>
<p>Suruglu	    14/8	  sunflower meal    973     Europe</p>
<p>Bonsay	     17/8	  wheat	    45,000     U.S.</p>
